WEBVTT

00:12:27.976 --> 00:12:31.330
and then the whispers
can grow thunderous over time

00:12:31.354 --> 00:12:34.070
if you're patient enough to explore it,

00:12:34.094 --> 00:12:36.458
almost in the way that a scientist would.

00:12:36.482 --> 00:12:38.097
So that's how it happens.

00:12:38.121 --> 00:12:41.296
CA: That novel is called
"The Signature of All Things."

00:12:41.320 --> 00:12:43.530
I have to say it's an amazing work.

00:12:43.554 --> 00:12:44.705
EG: Thank you.

00:12:44.729 --> 00:12:47.374
CA: I have a confession:
I never read "Eat Pray Love."

00:12:47.398 --> 00:12:51.453
EG: That's OK. You're not really
the demographic, Chris. No offense!

00:12:51.477 --> 00:12:52.779
CA: I did figure that out.

00:12:52.803 --> 00:12:56.755
But I did read "The Signature of All
Things," and I learned a lot in it,

00:12:56.779 --> 00:13:03.575
including this idea that is woven in there
about the connectedness of knowledge